+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+// SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project
+// Kimi K3.1 Pro EXL3 routed-expert MoE decode/medium-batch kernel for SM 8.0 (CMP 170HX).
+// Iteration 5 (Final Architecture):
+//   - Decoupled 5-launch pipeline so the hot EXL3 GEMM kernels carry ZERO cold epilogue
+//     registers, ZERO __threadfence(), ZERO partial-done atomics, and ZERO shared memory:
+//       L1: route_and_gate_up_input (routing, [K3|K2|K1] queue, dynamic split-K, H128 input)
+//       L2: exl3_moe_gemm_kernel<GateUp> (56-64 regs, 32-36 warps/SM, 0 spills)
+//       L3: situ_and_down_input (L2 slice reduce + H128 + SituAndMul + global-scale down input)
+//       L4: exl3_moe_gemm_kernel<Down> (56-64 regs, 32-36 warps/SM, 0 spills, no per-block blk[])
+//       L5: down_h128_and_combine (L2 slice reduce + H128 + down_svh + weighted combine -> BF16)
+//   - Device-side adaptive split-K chosen directly from runtime unique expert count (tile_total):
+//     eliminates low-unique-expert plateaus under both 1-row decode AND skewed 4/8-row routing.
+//   - Unified dynamic warp work queue over [K3 | K2 | K1] sorted items: zero wave tails and
+//     zero mixed-bit bucket drains.
+//   - Deferred-linear mul1_packed decoder (ZERO HFMA2 in K-loop) + PRMT K2 bit extract;
+//     coalesced uint32 LDG + __shfl_sync for all three bit widths (K1/K2/K3).
+//
+// EXL3 trellis format and mul1 codec adapted from turboderp-org/exllamav3 (MIT License)
+// and vLLM sm_80 EXL3 MoE v2 (Apache-2.0); see plugins/sm80/licenses/exl3/{LICENSE,NOTICE}.
+
